   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Connectors",
     "texto": [
      "**Lorsque** (when), **pendant que** (while), **depuis que** (since), **tandis que** (whereas, while in contrast).",
      "Example: **Lorsque tu es là, nous mangeons** (when you are here, we eat)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Formation and use",
     "texto": [
      "The **futur antérieur** is formed with **avoir** or **être** in the future + past participle: **tu auras fini** (you will have finished).",
      "With **être**, the past participle agrees with the subject: **elle sera arrivée** (she will have arrived)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Dès que and the future",
     "texto": [
      "**Dès que** (as soon as) introduces an action that can happen just before another.",
      "For two future actions, use a future tense; if the first will be finished before the second, use the **futur antérieur**: **Dès que tu auras fini, je viendrai** (as soon as you finish, I'll come)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
